# Trivy ignore file — mirrors deny.toml [advisories.ignore] with a written
# rationale. Trivy scans Cargo.lock directly and reports GHSA IDs, so we
# list the GHSAs here (deny.toml uses RUSTSEC IDs for the same vulns).
#
# Format : one advisory ID per line ; blank lines and `#` comments allowed.

# ─── rustls-webpki 0.102.8 (transitive via serenity 0.12) ───────
# See deny.toml for the full rationale. Summary : CRL / name-constraint
# advisories on rustls-webpki 0.102.8, pulled via
# serenity 0.12 -> tokio-tungstenite 0.21 -> tokio-rustls 0.25 ->
# rustls 0.22 -> rustls-webpki 0.102.8. The Skilluv Discord bot's only
# TLS peer is gateway.discord.gg, whose cert doesn't exercise the
# affected CRL / custom-name-constraint code paths, so the impact
# reduces to zero for our deployment. Drop these once serenity ships
# a release on the rustls 0.23 chain.
